    "originalFile": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Google Antigravity 2.0\",\n    \"url\": \"https://antigravity.google\",\n    \"description\": \"Standalone desktop app for orchestrating multiple AI agents in parallel with scheduled background tasks, subagent workflows, and native integrations with AI Studio, Firebase, and Android. Breaks the 'prompt, wait, respond' pattern by letting agents run in the background on cron-like schedules. Enables full project context export from Google AI Studio to local development.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-05-22\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Google just separated the agent manager from the IDE and shipped it as its own desktop app.\",\n      \"The cron-like scheduling piece is what I want to understand better. If I schedule a refactor agent to run at 2am, what happens when it hits a decision that needs human judgment?\",\n      \"Parallel agents are powerful, but the monitoring layer is what makes this actually usable.\",\n      \"The subagent workflow is where it gets interesting: running parallel agents without babysitting each one.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"TestSprite 3.0\",\n    \"url\": \"https://testsprite.com\",\n    \"description\": \"Autonomous end-to-end testing agent that uses parallel AI agents to explore apps, generate comprehensive test suites for frontend and backend, and auto-heal tests. Features include a parallel exploration fleet (dozens of agents mapping apps before tests are written), complex integration testing with dynamic variables, Data Flow debugging, and CLI integration for Claude Code/Codex users.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-05-23\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow-specific\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"The parallel exploration fleet is the part I want to poke at. If dozens of agents are clicking through a live app like real users before any test is written, they are also triggering real side effects\",\n      \"This is a really sick QA agent system. Seems like it goes way beyond Qodo / CodeRabbit.\",\n      \"Generating 50+ meaningful cases automatically is a massive jump compared to traditional approaches.\",\n      \"The CLI integration for claude code and codex users sounds exciting for developer workflows.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenHuman\",\n    \"url\": \"https://tinyhumans.ai/openhuman\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source AI harness that is local-first, privacy-first, with persistent memory across sessions using a Memory Tree with canonicalization, temporal metadata, and source authority scoring. Integrates with 118+ tools including Gmail, Slack, Telegram, Notion, and GitHub. Features tool calling with chaining, a code sandbox, and achieved 8000+ GitHub stars in first 7 days.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-05-15\",\n    \"category\": \"open-source agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"The privacy angle is a big reason to go local-first, but the persistent memory is what actually makes it usable day to day.\",\n      \"I am tired of re-explaining my tech stack and project goals every single time I open a new session.\",\n      \"Once an agent actually remembers your world, your preferences, your projects, your people, you stop thinking of it as a tool you use. It becomes context you live inside.\",\n      \"8000+ GitHub stars, 5000+ users in the first 7 days.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"buildpipe\",\n    \"url\": \"https://buildpipe.com\",\n    \"description\": \"Local-first pipeline automation app for developers that chains shell commands, AI calls, HTTP requests, and file operations into reusable pipelines. Trigger pipelines on schedule, file change, or webhook. Features AI Build to describe pipelines in plain English, 48 templates, encrypted API keys stored locally, and no telemetry or accounts required.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-05-23\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Think of it as a local Zapier or n8n, built specifically for developers.\",\n      \"AI calls introduce non-determinism into the pipeline which changes how you think about error handling and retry logic.\",\n      \"Multi-step AI workflows are powerful when they include clear checkpoints.\",\n      \"This looks super clean. Love the direction you're taking with AI workflows.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]"
  }
}

